* bevy-explorer: CI reuses the cached vendored Bevy build until its files change

Cargo judges a path dependency fresh by file times, and a checkout makes every file
new, so every native job of every run rebuilt the vendored Bevy, changed or not; git
and crates.io dependencies are judged by version and stay cached.

tooling/bevy-mtimes.py records each vendored file's blob id and time (floored to whole
seconds, which any cache archive keeps) into every profile's .fingerprint directory, so
the record travels in the same rust-cache archive as the artifacts. After the next
checkout it gives every unchanged file its recorded time back; changed files keep the
checkout's time and rebuild what depends on them. To Cargo this is a checkout that
never moved, so its own freshness rules stay correct. No extra cache entries or
requests.

Wired into every job that caches the explorer's target: Test Suite, Headless Smoke,
Clippy and the web target cache (whose key now hashes Bevy too), desktop, headless
packages and scenes. A change to the script selects every CI lane.

